	(text "FujiNet for the Atari 7800 - Rev0 (RP2354B).  Read from the cartridge slot outward: the console's 32-pin slot ->\nthe RP2354B on the 5V cart bus (boot block, mailbox, POKEY, and the PIO slot table) with the 512K SRAM it pages and\nthe 74HCT glue that decodes the console's address for it -> ESP32-S3 (FujiNet, WiFi, microSD) -> USB-C / CP2102N.\nPower (rails only): console 5V via a P-FET and USB VBUS via an SS34 meet on +5V; +3V3 buck (S3, SD, bridge);\n+3V3_RP LDO (every RP2354B supply pin, rises with the console's 5V).\nRP pin map: fujinet-firmware pico/atari-7800 a78_cart.h + a78map.h; S3 pin map: fujiversal-atari7800.h; glue:\na78_cartsel / a78_glue_oe / _we / _a8 (tools/check_nets.py and tools/check_glue.py hold the netlist to them).\nEdge: 18 positions with key slots at 3 and 16; pins 1-16 on the component side, facing the console's rear."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
